#### Interaction 2: Automated Alerting from Structured Logs

This sequence shows how structured logs enable real-time alerting on specific error patterns.

1. **Error logs generated**: Claims Service encounters database connection timeouts, logs errors:
   ```json
   {
     "timestamp": "2026-01-09T16:45:23.456Z",
     "severity": "ERROR",
     "service_name": "claims-service",
     "correlation_id": "CORR-2026-01-09-XYZ789",
     "event_type": "database_error",
     "error_type": "connection_timeout",
     "database_host": "claims-db-primary.prod.gainwell.com",
     "timeout_seconds": 30
   }
   ```
2. **Elasticsearch indexes logs**: Logs ingested and indexed within 5 seconds
3. **Alert rule evaluation**: Elasticsearch Watcher evaluates alert rule every 1 minute:
   ```json
   {
     "trigger": {
       "schedule": { "interval": "1m" }
     },
     "input": {
       "search": {
         "request": {
           "indices": ["logs-*"],
           "body": {
             "query": {
               "bool": {
                 "must": [
                   { "term": { "severity": "ERROR" }},
                   { "term": { "service_name": "claims-service" }},
                   { "term": { "error_type": "connection_timeout" }},
                   { "range": { "timestamp": { "gte": "now-5m" }}}
                 ]
               }
             },
             "aggs": {
               "error_count": { "value_count": { "field": "correlation_id" }}
             }
           }
         }
       }
     },
     "condition": {
       "compare": { "ctx.payload.aggregations.error_count.value": { "gt": 10 }}
     },
     "actions": {
       "page_ops_team": {
         "pagerduty": {
           "summary": "Claims Service Database Timeout Alert",
           "severity": "error",
           "details": {
             "error_count": "{{ctx.payload.aggregations.error_count.value}}",
             "service": "claims-service",
             "database": "claims-db-primary.prod.gainwell.com"
           }
         }
       }
     }
   }
   ```
4. **Alert fires**: PagerDuty incident created when >10 timeout errors in 5 minutes
5. **Enriched incident**: PagerDuty incident includes structured data from logs (database host, error count, time window)
6. **Instant investigation**: On-call engineer queries `service_name:claims-service AND error_type:connection_timeout AND timestamp:[now-1h TO now]` to see error pattern timeline

