#### Pitfall 4: Missing Correlation IDs in Async Processing

**Problem**: Background jobs and message queue consumers don't have correlation IDs from original request.

**Result**: Cannot trace asynchronous processing back to triggering request.

**Solution**:
- Include correlation ID in message payload/headers when publishing to queue
- Extract and set correlation ID in consumer before processing
- If no correlation ID exists, generate new one for the async workflow

**Example (RabbitMQ):**
```csharp
// Publisher
var correlationId = HttpContext.Items["CorrelationId"].ToString();
var properties = channel.CreateBasicProperties();
properties.CorrelationId = correlationId;
channel.BasicPublish("claims-exchange", "claim-submitted", properties, body);

// Consumer
var correlationId = ea.BasicProperties.CorrelationId;
using (LogContext.PushProperty("correlation_id", correlationId))
{
    await ProcessClaimAsync(message);
}
```
